Notes on the reasoning that shapes the reject-everything units (1, 3, 5): each has 4 fused sentences requiring 3 splits to fully resolve, but every listed candidate applies at most 2 breaks — so every candidate leaves at least one line with two complete sentences still fused, which fails "one sentence per line" regardless of how carefully placed the breaks that *are* there are. None is a complete repair, so I rejected all and supplied the full split under `missing`. Units 2, 4, 6, 7, 8 each had a candidate (or two) that fully resolved the fused sentences without severing any clause, so those got a normal accept/choose.
